{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty","id":818234,"title":"Non-charming uses of Majesty","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-27T23:27:41-08:00","id":818234,"title":"Non-charming uses of Majesty","content":"So majesty is meant as the power of supernatural charisma, right? The first power lets you use your dots in Majesty for all presence-based rolls. The common usage, of course, is becoming the super sexy vampire of legend and wowing everyone with how cool you are.<br /> <br /> But the book doesn't say &quot;all presence rolls based around being charming.&quot; It just says &quot;all presence rolls.&quot; So, RAW majesty could allow me to become, say, supernaturally imposing for a presence+intimidation roll.<br /> <br /> Would this be a valid use of the power though? It definitely makes sense, even in-universe, that majesty would let you do this, becoming an overly imposing figure in your victim's mind. At the same time though, it's not quite in the spirit of what the power is about, and I feel like it's kind of stepping on Nightmare's toes a bit. Like if Majesty can make you scary, then Nightmare becomes a little less special.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:21:36-08:00","id":818255,"title":"","content":"It certainly seems like it. I mean, Raphael LaDue in Chicago's Majesty just makes him seem much more cool and authoritative. Authoritative people are intimidating. It's not intimidating in the way that Nightmare is, but it's because Nightmare is <i>terrifying</i>.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I think that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:51:24-08:00","id":818268,"title":"","content":"I dislike such use, just because that means that a Majesty vampire will not be interested in buying Nightmare, since he can solve the problems with Majesty just as well. (well besides later dots, but dumping XP to get dots later in the future... doesn't feel that cool to me). However, by RAW, it seems that yes, it's all Presence rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:54:54-08:00","id":818270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818268#post818268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike such use, just because that means that a Majesty vampire will not be interested in buying Nightmare, since he can solve the problems with Majesty just as well. (well besides later dots, but dumping XP to get dots later in the future... doesn't feel that cool to me). However, by RAW, it seems that yes, it's all Presence rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my thinking. Like even beyond that concern, if someone else in the group makes a nosferatu and then sees that the Daeva can not only be charming, but also just as scary as him, he's probably gonna feel more than a little cheated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T01:07:22-08:00","id":818277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818270#post818270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's my thinking. Like even beyond that concern, if someone else in the group makes a nosferatu and then sees that the Daeva can not only be charming, but also just as scary as him, he's probably gonna feel more than a little cheated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> assuming someone creates a Nosferatu after seeing that in the first place... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T02:02:49-08:00","id":818294,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that while Majesty <b>can </b>apply to intimidation Awe's base effect is to always paint the Vampire in a positive light. So a Daeva looming over you doing his level best to make you shit yourself in terror will be bent into the awesome authority figure who, at some level, you respect for his powerful demeanor.Scary? yes, for certain values of scared. Scary enough to cause someone to hallucinate, lose their will, and run screaming in thoughtless terror leaving their loved ones to be consumed? Not really, so it won't be unseating Nightmare in the scares department.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T02:33:38-08:00","id":818306,"title":"","content":"Also because, with awe you add dice to your roll, with second level of nightmare, if you win the contested roll, you let the target run away automatically. The first power of nightmare probably is more a roleplaing effect then a ruled one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T03:10:19-08:00","id":818316,"title":"","content":"The first power of nightmare adds Nightmare to Intimidate rolls, just like Awe adds to Presence ones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> as for hallucinations and shit.. yeah... but would you really be buying a dot of nightmare just for the hallucinations? When you can do intimidation already with Majesty? <br /> Unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T03:18:52-08:00","id":818319,"title":"","content":"To be fair, if your story-teller is the lenient type and lets you combine the two, that'd be a really potent combination","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T04:50:44-08:00","id":818335,"title":"","content":"That's what Cross-Contamination devotion is for. And I guess different types of other devotions which combine the two powers for the ultimate feeling control","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:46:50-08:00","id":818389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like it's kind of stepping on Nightmare's toes a bit. Like if Majesty can make you scary, then Nightmare becomes a little less special.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? </div> </div> </div> I think you're misunderstanding Nightmare's thematic role. Nightmare isn't a &quot;I become super intimidating!&quot; power. Sure, the first dot does give a bit of a bonus towards doing that, but that's not quite the only benefit of Dread Presence. Dread Presence creates <i>illusions</i>. They have to be creepy illusions that stem from controlled mental hallucinations, mind, but still they're still illusions. You can walk around under Obfuscate, using Dread Presence, and freak the ever living shit out of people. Anyone who likes playing illusionist characters can tell you that a well timed illusion or distraction can a hell of a lot. And its free. There's no cost to messing with people like this (beyond the social). There's no save, no way to resist the illusions, not even with Lashing Out. Lashing Out cancels the Intimidation bonus, but doesn't touch the illusions.<br /> <br /> That big about Obfuscate is actually a huge, huge difference between Majesty and Nightmare. Majesty you have to be seen. With Nightmare? You're often better off <i>unseen</i>.<br /> <br /> The second dot inflicts the Frightened Condition; this is the &quot;Run Away From Scary Face!&quot; power that Nightmare had as its first and third dot in 1e. Execpt, again, you don't need to show your actual face. This is almost more of combat ability, preventing someone from engaging in a fight, or not letting them approach somewhere. Third dot inflicts the Delusional Condition. Delusional is like Dementation in a single power. You have a break from reality and have some insane belief driving you that's clearly not true. It can be something as simple as inflicting germophobia, or it can be something like suddenly thinking all your friends and loved ones are out to kill you. You're effectively changing people's fundamental beliefs, not asking favors. And, again, this is all from not being seen.<br /> <br /> The fourth dot creates a massive illusion that can affect a large group of people. While its aimed at being scary (thus, Nightmare), its uses far exceed anything related to social maneuvering, like Majesty does. The Fifth dot is an attack power. You <i>damage people</i> and turn them into Broken husks of their former selves. That's nothing to sneer at.<br /> <br /> Awe may be useful as an intimidation roll. But all this works with the Majesty user as the center of attention, directing everything with quiet words and whispers, or perhaps an impassioned speech. Majesty is always all about the user as the center of attention while in plain sight. Nightmare? Nightmare's primary use is to make people question reality and lose their ability to form rational thoughts.<br /> <br /> The intimidation bonus is a point of overlap, sure. And using both Dread Presence and Awe together can give you a really high Presence+Intimidate dice pool (which sounds better than it actually is, given how Social Maneuvering works). But that's only half of a power - and, even then, you can use the Dread Presence Intimidation bonus while hidden and creating illusions. And that's the only point of overlap. The two powers have completely different directions they run in.<br /> <br /> Cross Contamination and Wet Dream are also both unique in their execution. Cross Contamination, as a power, is used to force people to pay attention to you; do not make the mistake thinking that its just a devotion mixing the Awe+Dread Presence effects. Its like the Nelapsi devotion Churchtower Gaze. They can't look away, and they suffer penalties to perception checks. That's pretty awesome. Wet Dream, likewise, has some interesting effects, inflicting both Spooked and Swooning; despite the name, spooked doesn't necessarily imply fear, but rather you have a hyper focus on something that holds your interest that you'd rather check out than live out your mundane lifestyle. When combined with Swooning, its a great way to drive people into your arms for a bite to eat at night. Its the classic &quot;vampire visits dream, you see them outside, and go out, and get bit, don't know what compelled you&quot; image. Awesome hunting tool.<br /> <br /> EDIT - So, lets TL;DR this. In short, no. Neither Majesty nor Nightmare is about being scary. Majesty is about highly visible emotional-based crowd control, Nightmare is about freakish hallucinations, best used under Obfuscate. The two are just too different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-28-2016, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:04:00-08:00","id":818393,"title":"","content":"You can't use both Awe and Dread Presence at once. Also, my main argument was that a person who's highly specialized in Majesty, will not want to dip into Nightmare.. and going deep costs a lot too.<br /> <br /> That's the basic gist of it, you lose half a power, and so, as a Majesty user, it's more worthwhile to spend your hard earned XP elsewhere to gain moar. unless of course you want those higher level nightmare powers hard, and that desire overpowers the wasted point of XP or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:17:51-08:00","id":818401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818393#post818393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't use both Awe and Dread Presence at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that written?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818393#post818393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, my main argument was that a person who's highly specialized in Majesty, will not want to dip into Nightmare.. and going deep costs a lot too.<br /> <br /> That's the basic gist of it, you lose half a power, and so, as a Majesty user, it's more worthwhile to spend your hard earned XP elsewhere to gain moar. unless of course you want those higher level nightmare powers hard, and that desire overpowers the wasted point of XP or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. In my opinion, the bonus to Intimidation is the least useful part of Dread Presence. And since it adds your Nightmare dots to Intimidation rolls, a Majesty-focused character who only wants to dip into Nightmare for one dot could get the same bonus to Intimidation for half the XP just by <i>buying a dot of Intimidation</i>. Or, heck, for a single measy XP they could buy an Intimidation specialty for &quot;with Majesty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:41:37-08:00","id":818416,"title":"","content":"It's written in the write up for Dread Presence. The powers are only supposed to apply to normal intimidation rolls only, not supernaturally augmented ones. Awe has a similar restriction but since it only specifically cites Majesty as a power it doesn't stack with, rules lawyers take that and run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:56:28-08:00","id":818424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818393#post818393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't use both Awe and Dread Presence at once.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, you can. Cross contamination does not suggest that you cannot have DP and Awe together, only that you can't have CC and DP/Awe up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, my main argument was that a person who's highly specialized in Majesty, will not want to dip into Nightmare.. and going deep costs a lot too. </div> </div> </div> And I disagree. Nightmare and Majesty work awesome together. They both key off the same attributes and skill (Empathy), so there's a lot of synergy there there; there are two devotions that are pretty kick ass in the right situations. Hint of Fear makes an awesome addition to any Daeva combatant, alongside Enfeebling Aura. <br /> <br /> Now, I won't suggest that someone who's gone deep into Majesty will want more than 2 dots of Nightmare. But its not because the two powers are too similar, its because they're too different; I don't feel there's real synergy beyond that second dot. I'm sure that there are concepts out there that will involve it, but its not instictive for me. But dipping for two dots of Nightmare? Oh, hells yes. Do want. I can see lots of Daeva drooling over getting up to Nightmare 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the basic gist of it, you lose half a power, and so, as a Majesty user, it's more worthwhile to spend your hard earned XP elsewhere to gain moar. unless of course you want those higher level nightmare powers hard, and that desire overpowers the wasted point of XP or so. </div> </div> </div> Even if you couldn't use the Intimidateion bonus with Awe... I wouldn't call it half a dot. The main benefit of Dread Presence are the illusions, not some piddly +1 social bonus to an occasionally used skill (2e promotes using a variety of skills, so you won't be spamming Intimidate all the time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:02:09-08:00","id":818427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818416#post818416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's written in the write up for Dread Presence. The powers are only supposed to apply to normal intimidation rolls only, not supernaturally augmented ones. Awe has a similar restriction but since it only specifically cites Majesty as a power it doesn't stack with, rules lawyers take that and run.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummm..... yeah, I'm going to disagree here too. I'm fairly sure that the &quot;mundane Intimidation rolls&quot; refers to the idea that you can't use Nightmare's or Majesty's social bonuses with Discipline or other magical powers that use those skills. So, no adding Majesty and Nightmare dots again to the invocation of Mortal Terror (Presence + Intimidation + Nightmare), but yes to adding them both to a non-power dice pools like social maneuvering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:04:56-08:00","id":818430,"title":"","content":"<br /> Nightmare 1 is for the reflexive illusions and shutting down the opponent's ability to use willpower to boost dicepools.<br /> Nightmare 2 lets you make people run.<br /> Nightmare 3 lets you shape their beliefs.<br /> Nightmare 4 creates illusions.<br /> Nightmare 5 is a psychic attack.<br /> <br /> Majesty 1 lets you ignore all social penalties (for i.e. just killing someone's best friend), distract everyone, and summon people.<br /> Majesty 2 lets you Charm people.<br /> Majesty 3 lets you mass play with emotions.<br /> Majesty 4 lets you Enthrall people.<br /> Majesty 5 creates a magic &quot;don't mess with me&quot; shield of dubious actual value.<br /> <br /> There is not much overlap here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-28-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:23:41-08:00","id":818441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818430#post818430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Majesty 5 creates a magic &amp;quot;don't mess with me&amp;quot; shield of dubious actual value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to drift too far off topic here, but if you're looking at Idol as a &quot;don't touch me&quot; shield, I'm not surprised it looks dubious. That's what Soverignty was for, but Idol serves a very different purpose. It's main role is as a way to bring everyone in the room a bit further under your sway at once. All of your thralls become so enamoured they can't even spend Willpower to resist you. Everyone you have Charmed moves up a level to Enthralled. And even the people you havevent brought into the fold yet are hesitant to act against you. It's purpose isn't to make you untouchable, it's to make you the object of everyone's adoration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:56:34-08:00","id":818531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818441#post818441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to drift too far off topic here, but if you're looking at Idol as a &quot;don't touch me&quot; shield, I'm not surprised it looks dubious. That's what Soverignty was for, but Idol serves a very different purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ehhh.... not exactly.... There's three parts to Idol - one is a ban on taking any action (physical or social) that could harm the vampire unless you pass a Resolve+BP-Majesty roll. The second part is upgrading anyone who's been Charmed to Enthralled with a failed Res+BP-Maj roll (note that Enthralled requires a willpower expendature and Humanity check to try and do something vampire doesn't want, like hurt him). The third is a ban on Enthralled people from being able to spend willpower to act against you (note that its &quot;act against&quot; not &quot;resist&quot;). All three involve some measure of not hurting the vampire in some way.<br /> <br /> Now, the upgraded Charmed to Enthralled includes more than just not harming the vampire, but it still includes it. So, I kind of have to side with SoulGambit on this one. And I must agree with the dubious part. Indomitable is going to be a fairly common merit in Vampire games, I imagine, giving even low BP/Resolve characters a good chance at resisting. And don't get me started on Strength of Resolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-28-2016, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:05:27-08:00","id":818546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818268#post818268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike such use, just because that means that a Majesty vampire will not be interested in buying Nightmare, since he can solve the problems with Majesty just as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be true for a vampire for you, but I do not think that is the case for ALL vampires. Cross-contamination is a pretty neat devotion so a vampire with both Majesty and Nightmare could have access to that. Those are my personal two favorite disciplines, so even though I might have one on my vampire, I still might be inclined to take the other. <br /> <br /> There are different types of intimidation and Majesty makes you the queen bee and sometimes the queen bee can be intimidating. I see no problems with that. Since Nightmare is so entirely different than Majesty ( as someone pointed out), if a vampire was branching out, I dont see why it wouldnt be a viable options to take. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:23:12-08:00","id":818557,"title":"","content":"Looking at Majesty 5 in more detail. The Resolve + Blood Potency roll to attack the vampire at least gets a -5 penalty from Majesty 5, so it isn't completely useless. Confidant is also free, while Loyalty costs 2v per use, so the AoE aspect actually does become useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:29:02-08:00","id":818560,"title":"","content":"Chance die for like the vast majority of mortals and zeroing out most BP1-2 vampires ain't bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:41:56-08:00","id":818567,"title":"","content":"That and the fact that every one the vampire has Charmed or Enthralled will leap unquestioningly to his aid the moment violence is insinuated against him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:14:26-08:00","id":818590,"title":"","content":"Oh, absolutely. Idol works excellently against mortals, ghouls and the young / inexperienced vampires. I would also argue that it works against animals, which makes it an excellent defense against certain Animalism abilities, and ephemeral beings / strix, edging out the weaker of those beings as well. You've edged out the mooks, basically; potentially turned some of them into allies. The issue isn't that Idol is useless; its that its situational and you have to know your targets. That's where the dubious comes in - you're never quite sure if its working with some people. Of course, the reverse is true as well - Its good for turning a potential combat situation into one where people aren't sure if they want to commit, because you can never tell if you'll be able to attack.<br /> <br /> Another situation where Majesty is different from Nightmare - Majesty, even as a scary threat, turns things from combat to socializing. Nightmare confuses and disorients people so they don't know what's going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:04:07-08:00","id":818664,"title":"","content":"Well, unless the affected character's Resolve + Blood Potency equals ten or more, I still think Idol is pretty worth it as a defensive combat power. Say someone with a sum of nine tries to battle me, after the penalty for Majesty they still end up dropping roughly every fourth attack (four dice gives roughly 76% chance of one success), unless they spend Willpower, but then those are points they cannot spend to actually harm me. That is all right in my book and over the course of a longer fight the two Vitae and one Willpower would probably pay off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}